classDiagram
    direction LR

    class AcademicActor {
        <<external — academic>>
    }
    class School {
        <<external — academic>>
    }

    class AlertType {
        +Int alertTypeId
        +String code
        +String name
        +Severity severity
        +Channel channel
    }

    class Severity {
        <<enumeration>>
        INFO
        WARNING
        CRITICAL
    }

    class Channel {
        <<enumeration>>
        DASHBOARD
        EMAIL
        PUSH
    }

    class Alert {
        +Long alertId
        +Long academicActorId
        +Int alertTypeId
        +DateTime raisedAt
        +DateTime resolvedAt
        +raise()
        +resolve()
    }

    class AcademicConfiguration {
        +Int configurationId
        +Int schoolId
        +String configurationName
        +String configurationValue
        +String description
    }

    class SecurityConfiguration {
        +Int configurationId
        +String configurationName
        +String configurationValue
        +String description
    }

    AlertType "1" --> "0..*" Alert : alert.alert_type_id FK
    Alert --> Severity
    AlertType --> Channel

    Alert ..> AcademicActor : academic_actor_id — cross-context, no FK
    AcademicConfiguration ..> School : school_id — cross-context, no FK

    note for Alert "RN-42: alerts are system-generated for defined event types. RN-43: resolution requires the appropriate permission. resolvedAt NULL = unresolved. No code raises channel=EMAIL alerts today — only the password-recovery e-mail flow sends mail (see c1-system-context.mmd)."
    note for AcademicConfiguration "Scoped per school (uq_academic_configuration on school_id + configuration_name), e.g. tardy_tolerance_minutes."
    note for SecurityConfiguration "Global (no school_id), uq on configuration_name, e.g. max_login_attempts, session_timeout_minutes, lockout_duration_minutes. Password policy lives in identity.password_policy, not here."
    note "All classes also carry the standard audit block (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and `06-data/domains/07-notification.md` / `08-configuration.md` for the column-level ER view."
